[-] Move Habits into habits files (Decision 57) =core-habit ~ $Parent of the Habit child chain (core-habit-pins through core-habit-ship): read Habits from <charter>.habits.actions, stamp occurrences, project them to recurring VEVENTs and merge calendar edits back. Done when every child lands, each independently reviewed. Open: =habit-cancel-marker, =habit-unrecur-no-open.$ !2 ^2026-10-11T17:51 <spec-habits #01a12c17-0314-7f10-8628-3f27adcb36ac
    >[x] Implement native Habit graph and schema conformance =core-habit-graph $Native Habit identity, state, rule and graph projection, conformant to specification v0.5.0 (Core 18e8f91).$ !2 ^2026-10-26T05:15 %2026-11-04T07:38 <core-habit-pins #01a176a3-0d30-72d0-a5a2-9813d611c428
    >[x] Classify habits files in every reader and archive path =core-habit-readers $Every reader and archive path classifies habits files; R: outside a habits file survives writes (Core 985249d, nvim 89a6099).$ !2 ^2026-10-26T05:15 %2026-11-05T09:30 <core-habit-graph #01a176a3-0d3d-75f2-931d-cad677f00dd7
    >[x] Make Habit slot identity independent of device zone =core-habit-slots $Device-zone-independent Habit slot keys and occurrence and step UUIDs, as a tested library (Core ea55522).$ !2 ^2026-10-26T05:15 %2026-11-05T10:24 <core-habit-readers #01a176a3-0d4c-7153-91c2-bf858dd261d4
    >[x] Stamp templates with stable step identity =core-habit-steps $Add a pure Core function that stamps (Habit, template forest, NativeSlot) into an occurrence tree, with step ids derived from persisted template-step UUIDs, plus a merge that never overwrites or duplicates an existing id. Refuse steps with no written id. Done when the habit_step_identity tests pass.$ !2 ^2026-10-26T05:15 %2026-11-27T21:28 <core-habit-slots #01a176a3-0d5a-78e0-b818-bafe89a5fc3a
        >>[x] Keep written-id records when reading a named template =chst-reader $The named-template reader returns its steps with which ones had a written id, from the parser's source map, so stamping can refuse unminted steps (Core tests 6d2be36, implementation 73952d5).$ !2 +steward ^2026-11-07T18:00 %2026-11-07T19:28 #01a1b72b-6f4b-7e93-b3cc-b456bbae6cdb
        >>[x] Stamp a template as one remap, refusing recurrence and ancestor dependencies =chst-stamp $Write the stamping function as one pass that maps step ids, predecessor links, plan_id and external_occurrence_key. Refuse, naming file and line, templates with R: (E002), steps waiting on an ancestor (E009) and steps without a written id. Waits on =template-recurrence-approve. Done when habit_step_identity and each refusal pass.$ !2 +steward ^2026-11-07T18:00 %2026-11-27T21:28 <chst-reader <template-recurrence-approve <template-recurrence-pins #01a1b72b-6f67-7c31-a094-82256125c718
        >>[x] Place stamped child times in a DST gap by canonical_slot's before-gap rule =chst-dst $A stamped step's zoned time that falls in a DST gap should resolve the way canonical_slot does (ics_schedule_spec.md). Done when a test stamps Los Angeles 2026-03-08 02:30 as 10:30Z, and a fall-back overlap case and an ordinary day pass unchanged.$ !2 +steward ^2026-11-07T18:00 %2026-11-27T21:28 <chst-stamp #01a1b72b-6f80-7961-a9ef-916e962ee623
    >[x] Generate every arrived Habit slot in resumable batches =core-habit-catchup $Replace the single-live token with write-path catch-up that generates every arrived, non-excluded slot exactly once in resumable batches and reports any backlog. Done when habit_catchup tests cover missed slots, tiny budgets, interrupted writes and retry.$ !2 ^2026-10-26T05:15 %2026-11-27T21:28 <core-habit-steps #01a176a3-0d68-7452-8252-1c5ca5398a9e
    >[x] Suppress generation against live and archived occurrences =core-habit-dedup $Check live and archived occurrence lineage before generating, so a completed or cancelled slot is never regenerated, without adding archive data to live views. Done when habit_archive_dedup tests pass and archive files stay unchanged.$ !2 ^2026-10-26T05:15 %2026-11-27T21:28 <core-habit-catchup #01a176a3-0d78-7d52-9ab4-4b9b34d095b4
    >[x] Preserve occurrence history through rule edits =core-habit-rules $When a recurrence rule or template is edited, generate newly due slots once and leave existing Actions, ids, states and archived lineage unchanged. Done when habit_rule_history tests cover frequency, start, exclusion and template edits.$ !2 ^2026-10-26T05:15 %2026-11-28T01:04 <core-habit-dedup #01a176a3-0d87-7231-ace6-6438e0d41c09
    >[ ] Project Habits and merge series and occurrence edits =core-habit-projection $Write recurring VEVENTs to plans/ and merge calendar edits back: series edits go to the Habit line and RECURRENCE-ID edits go to the Action. Done when habit_calendar_roundtrip passes, including moved occurrences keyed by RECURRENCE-ID and non-IANA TZIDs either mapped or refused with a clear error.$ !2 ^2026-10-26T05:15 <core-habit-rules #01a176a3-0d96-7910-9b46-d3a93e3e6aa7
    >[ ] Apply explicit same-UID kind-change proposals =core-habit-conversion $Detect same-UID kind changes against the merge base and let the user accept, revert or defer them, with --accept-all for scripts. Done when habit_kind_change tests every outcome, with no duplicate Actions and dependencies kept.$ !2 ^2026-10-26T05:15 <core-habit-projection #01a176a3-0da5-7b82-93fb-9d99e7fddae8
    >[ ] Hold UID replacements and require explicit linking =core-habit-links $Hold calendar events whose UID was replaced or split, and require an explicit link instead of matching identities automatically. Doctor diagnoses and --fix uses the same link. Done when habit_uid_link tests pass. --accept-all never skips link confirmation.$ !2 ^2026-10-26T05:15 <core-habit-conversion #01a176a3-0db5-77a0-a07b-b6341c0de6b8
    >[ ] Rewrite existing vdir Habits once with restart-safe migration =core-habit-migration $Provide a previewable one-time conversion of existing vdir Habits into habits files. It must be safe to interrupt and retry, and a no-op once done. Done when habit_migration tests pass and sources survive a failed run.$ !2 ^2026-10-26T05:15 <core-habit-links #01a176a3-0dc4-7ed3-b0d0-44744df781c0
    >[ ] Validate and release the complete Habit implementation cycle =core-habit-ship $Release the Habit cycle: full Core gate, spec conformance and platform validate-pinned pass, nvim reader tests land, and real CLI catch-up, edit, sync, archive and doctor run against a fixture workspace. Then move platform pins to the released tags and close core-habit, slot-key-zone and grammar-habits.$ !2 ^2026-10-26T05:15 <core-habit-migration #01a176a3-0dd4-74c1-b4b5-16880111bc6c
[ ] Test where calendar clients leave a series that loses its recurrence =unrecur-series-test $On a synced collection, make a daily event that started weeks ago, remove its recurrence on the phone and in khal, sync, and read DTSTART. If clients keep the series start, accepting recurring -> one-off would pull the live occurrence's block back to it, and the kind-change proposal must show that. Same setup as x-prop-survival; run them together.$ !3 +calendar ^2026-10-11T17:51 <resume-calendar-sync #01a12c17-0320-7781-acee-d760d918d609
